# Two terminals, one above the other: exactly one filled cursor.
#
# A terminal emulator fills the focused surface's cursor and hollows out
# every other one — which is how you tell, at a glance, which shell your
# typing reaches. mnml paints into cells, so `ui.pty_cursor.unfocused`
# decides what an unfocused pane gets. The default `hollow` keeps the
# cell's character readable in the cursor colour; the cell a shell
# leaves its cursor on is blank, so an outline stands in for one.
#
# WHICH outline depends on the face. With MnmlSymbols installed it is
# U+F2001, the full-cell rectangle mnml bakes (`glyph/builder.zig`) to
# match what ghostty draws in pixels; without it, the Unicode fallback
# `▯`. What this script asserts is `▯`, for two reasons that both hold:
# the corpus driver does not fire the `startup` hook, so the font scan
# that would answer the question never runs here at all; and
# `MNML_FONT_DIRS=` gives the run no font directories either way, so it
# stays `▯` on a machine with the face installed and on one without.
# The other three squares of that matrix (face present, and both under
# --ascii) are pinned as unit tests in `ui/pty_view.zig`. What none of
# them can see is the baked glyph's actual pixels.
#
# The colours are the only way a script can see focus at all: a filled
# cursor and an ordinary cell hold the same character. #abb2bf is
# onedark's foreground — the colour a terminal uses for the cursor when
# the child has not asked (OSC 12) for another — and #1e222a its ground.
#
# `sleep 30` keeps each child alive: an exited pane paints its banner
# over the last row and has no cursor at all.
# env: MNML_FONT_DIRS=
command view.toggle_tree
ex term printf LL; sleep 30
expect screen contains "LL"
ex term printf RR; sleep 30
expect screen contains "RR"

# // changed (pane-rail): every pane wears a one-cell rail down its
# left edge now, so each child's grid starts a column further in —
# column 3, not 2.
#
# The lower pane has focus: its cursor cell is filled — the cursor
# colour is the ground, so the cell is not the pane's own #1e222a.
expect color 3 21 bg #abb2bf
# The upper one is hollow: the outline, in the cursor colour, on the
# pane's own ground. Not filled.
expect screen contains "LL▯"
expect color 3 2 fg #abb2bf
expect color 3 2 bg #1e222a

# Click into the upper pane and the two swap — never two filled at once.
click 10 5
expect pane "printf LL"
expect color 3 2 bg #abb2bf
expect screen contains "RR▯"
expect color 3 21 fg #abb2bf
expect color 3 21 bg #1e222a
